---
// ============================================================================
// Comparison Sorting Demystified Guide (Route: /guides/sorting-algorithms/)
// ============================================================================

import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Comparison Sorting Demystified — Bubble, Selection & Insertion"
  description="Learn how Bubble Sort, Selection Sort, and Insertion Sort work, their swap mechanics, stability trade-offs, and why Insertion Sort excels on nearly sorted data."
  currentRoute="/guides/sorting-algorithms/"
>
  <div class="guide-article-container container">
    <nav class="breadcrumb-nav" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <ol class="breadcrumb-list">
        <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
        <li class="separator" aria-hidden="true">/</li>
        <li><a href="/guides/">Guides</a></li>
        <li class="separator" aria-hidden="true">/</li>
        <li aria-current="page">Sorting Demystified</li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <header class="article-header">
      <div class="badge-row">
        <span class="category-badge">SORTING ALGORITHMS</span>
        <span class="badge-pill">ELEMENTARY O(n²)</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="article-title">Comparison Sorting Demystified: Bubble, Selection & Insertion</h1>
      <p class="article-lead">
        Explore the mechanics, comparisons, swaps, stability, and algorithmic trade-offs of the three foundational comparison sorting algorithms.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Interactive Callout -->
    <div class="interactive-callout">
      <div class="callout-icon" aria-hidden="true">&gt;_</div>
      <div class="callout-content">
        <h2 class="callout-title">Interactive Tool Available</h2>
        <p class="callout-desc">Observe dynamic bar heights, swap counters, and pass animations live.</p>
      </div>
      <a href="/visualizers/sorting/" class="btn-callout">Launch Visualizer →</a>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 1: Algorithmic Comparison Matrix -->
    <section class="guide-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">1. The Three Elementary Sorts at a Glance</h2>
      <div class="table-scroll-wrapper">
        <table class="data-table" aria-label="Sorting Comparison Matrix">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Algorithm</th>
              <th scope="col">Best Time</th>
              <th scope="col">Worst Time</th>
              <th scope="col">Space</th>
              <th scope="col">Stable?</th>
              <th scope="col">Key Mechanism</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Bubble Sort</strong></td>
              <td><code>O(n)</code> (early exit)</td>
              <td><code>O(n²)</code></td>
              <td><code>O(1)</code></td>
              <td><span class="tag-stable">Yes</span></td>
              <td>Repeatedly swaps adjacent out-of-order elements</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Selection Sort</strong></td>
              <td><code>O(n²)</code></td>
              <td><code>O(n²)</code></td>
              <td><code>O(1)</code></td>
              <td><span class="tag-unstable">No</span></td>
              <td>Finds minimum element in unsorted portion; 1 swap per pass</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Insertion Sort</strong></td>
              <td><code>O(n)</code> (adaptive)</td>
              <td><code>O(n²)</code></td>
              <td><code>O(1)</code></td>
              <td><span class="tag-stable">Yes</span></td>
              <td>Inserts key into already-sorted left subarray</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 2: In-Depth Breakdowns -->
    <section class="guide-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">2. Deep-Dive: How Each Algorithm Works</h2>

      <div class="algo-breakdown-card">
        <h3 class="algo-name">Bubble Sort: Adjacent Comparisons</h3>
        <p class="algo-desc">
          Bubble Sort iterates through the array, comparing pairs of adjacent elements ($j$ and $j+1$). If an element is greater than its right neighbor, 
          they are swapped. By the end of pass $i$, the $i$-th largest element has "bubbled" to index $n - 1 - i$.
        </p>
        <p class="algo-tip">
          <strong>Optimization:</strong> By tracking whether any swaps occurred during a pass, the algorithm can terminate immediately if the array is already sorted, running in $O(n)$ time.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="algo-breakdown-card">
        <h3 class="algo-name">Selection Sort: Minimum Selection</h3>
        <p class="algo-desc">
          Selection Sort divides the array into a sorted prefix and an unsorted suffix. In each pass $i$, it scans the entire unsorted suffix $[i \dots n-1]$ 
          to find the index of the absolute minimum element, and then performs a single swap with index $i$.
        </p>
        <p class="algo-tip">
          <strong>Trade-off:</strong> It minimizes swaps to exactly <em>n &minus; 1</em>, but always performs <em>n(n &minus; 1) / 2</em> comparisons regardless of initial array ordering.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="algo-breakdown-card">
        <h3 class="algo-name">Insertion Sort: Online Adaptive Sorting</h3>
        <p class="algo-desc">
          Insertion Sort builds the sorted array one element at a time. It takes the current element (`key`) and shifts all greater elements in the sorted subarray to the right, 
          inserting `key` into its correct slot.
        </p>
        <p class="algo-tip">
          <strong>Production relevance:</strong> Because it takes only $O(n)$ comparisons on nearly-sorted data, it is used as the base case in hybrid algorithms like <em>Timsort</em> and <em>Introsort</em>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 3: Stability -->
    <section class="guide-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">3. Why Stability Matters</h2>
      <p class="guide-text">
        A sorting algorithm is <strong>stable</strong> if duplicate keys maintain their original relative order. For example, if you sort a list of students by Grade after already sorting by Name, 
        a stable sort preserves the alphabetical ordering of students who share the same grade.
      </p>
      <div class="stability-box">
        <p><strong>Selection Sort is Unstable:</strong> Consider sorting <code>[ (4, 'A'), (4, 'B'), (2, 'C') ]</code>. In pass 0, the minimum is 2, so <code>(4, 'A')</code> swaps with <code>(2, 'C')</code>. The resulting array is <code>[ (2, 'C'), (4, 'B'), (4, 'A') ]</code>, inverting the original order of the two 4s!</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="article-footer">
      <div class="footer-nav-row">
        <a href="/guides/binary-search/" class="footer-link-back">← Binary Search Guide</a>
        <a href="/guides/bfs-dfs/" class="footer-link-next">Next Guide: Graph Traversals (BFS vs DFS) →</a>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .guide-article-container {
    padding-top: var(--space-8);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-16);
    max-width: var(--reading-max);
  }

  .breadcrumb-nav { margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
  .breadcrumb-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    list-style: none;
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
  .breadcrumb-list a { color: var(--color-text-secondary); transition: color var(--transition-fast); }
  .breadcrumb-list a:hover { color: var(--color-primary-400); }
  .separator { color: var(--color-border); }

  .article-header { margin-bottom: var(--space-8); }
  .badge-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }
  .category-badge {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-primary-400);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }
  .badge-pill {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-brand-300);
    background-color: rgba(190, 229, 75, 0.1);
    border: 1px solid rgba(190, 229, 75, 0.25);
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }

  .article-title {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    line-height: var(--leading-tight);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }
  .article-lead {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }

  .interactive-callout {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(190, 229, 75, 0.1) 0%, rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.1) 100%);
    border: 1px solid rgba(190, 229, 75, 0.3);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: var(--space-5);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
  }
  .callout-icon { font-size: 2rem; }
  .callout-content { flex: 1; min-width: 200px; }
  .callout-title { font-size: var(--text-base); font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-text-primary); margin-bottom: 2px; }
  .callout-desc { font-size: var(--text-xs); color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .btn-callout {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-primary-text);
    background-color: var(--color-primary-600);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-primary-500);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 10px 16px;
    min-height: 40px;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    transition: all var(--transition-fast);
  }
  .btn-callout:hover { background-color: var(--color-primary-500); transform: translateY(-1px); }

  .guide-section { margin-bottom: var(--space-10); }
  .section-title {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-2);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
  }
  .guide-text {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .table-scroll-wrapper { overflow-x: auto; margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
  .data-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    text-align: left;
  }
  .data-table th {
    background-color: var(--color-bg-elevated);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .data-table td {
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
  }
  .data-table code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--color-emerald-400);
    background-color: rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.1);
    padding: 1px 4px;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }
  .tag-stable { color: var(--color-emerald-400); font-weight: 700; }
  .tag-unstable { color: #f87171; font-weight: 700; }

  .algo-breakdown-card {
    background-color: var(--color-bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-5);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }
  .algo-name {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }
  .algo-desc {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }
  .algo-tip {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--color-amber-400);
    background-color: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.08);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-amber-400);
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius-sm) var(--radius-sm) 0;
  }

  .stability-box {
    background-color: var(--color-bg-elevated);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-4);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }
  .stability-box code { font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--color-brand-300); }

  .article-footer {
    padding-top: var(--space-6);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }
  .footer-nav-row {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .footer-link-back { color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .footer-link-back:hover { color: var(--color-primary-400); }
  .footer-link-next { color: var(--color-primary-400); }
  .footer-link-next:hover { color: #ffffff; }
</style>
